      "purpose": "Check the limit of the first result.",
      "explanation": "At \u0394=1, E=2, \u03b5=1/4 and \u03b4=3/4, the exposition gives v3 \u2264 5/32 < 4/25 < v2 and V\u2082(3,S) < V\u2082(2,S) for 0\u2264S\u22649/400. Thus the adjacent smaller batch can win at positive calibrated noise. The transcript brackets and inclusive energy range have the supplied formal bindings. The average-only reversal is a separate conventional extension. The lower comparator is the squared Gaussian base standard deviation, identified with full batch through the fullbatch target.",
