      "purpose": "See what the calibrated variances mean.",
      "explanation": "The appendix establishes finite-horizon continuity, monotonicity, feasibility, and attainment for both profiles, and identifies the shared positive full-batch calibration through the Gaussian formula. That common reference is used in the finite comparison and the counterexample. The referenced exposition itself attributes the analytic Gaussian calibration formula to Balle and Wang (2018). Only the full-batch identification has a target binding here; continuity, attainment, the Gaussian formula and the average-only identification remain conventional components in the supplied assessments.",
