      "purpose": "Read how positivity moves across centers.",
      "explanation": "The stated lemma says a nonnegative gap at a smaller nonnegative center implies strict positivity at a larger center. It supplies the propagation step used when the low-rate boundary has been shown positive. The stored source-correspondence assessment distinguishes the source proof by a tilted strictly convex function from the exposition\u2019s Gaussian-kernel ratio argument.",
